{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "All's Well That Ends Well", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Together Like Always", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe emotions and feelings in present and past situations in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "spit it out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used to urge someone to say or confess something quickly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Ok. Peter spit it out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear when someone is angry.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "what's eating you?", "type": "name"}, {"content": "what is annoying or bothering you?", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What's eating you? Is it the trip?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Comparative Clause: Degree", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Comparisons express differences or similarities based on a judgement or standard of measurement.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you use comparative clauses, your English sounds more dynamic and mature.   </br></br>You introduce adverbial clauses of comparison of degree with the subordinating conjunction <span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"italic\">than</span></span>, or by the relative adverb <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">as</span><span class=\"italic\">.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: </br></br><span class=\"italic\">  I am older <span class=\"strong\">than my brother</span>. </br>He doesn't work harder <span class=\"strong\">than we do</span>.</br> My mother earns more <span class=\"strong\">than my father</span>.</br> He is as smart <span class=\"strong\">as he is handsome</span>.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes I feel I am more serious about this relationship <span class=\"strong\">than</span> you are.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You are more upset <span class=\"strong\">than</span> I expected about this.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Candace is as secretive <span class=\"strong\">as</span> she is intelligent.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "This may be less lucrative <span class=\"strong\">than</span> my other job, but rest assured it is much more rewarding and important.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">Comparative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">Meaning</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class = \\\"strong\\\">Example</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"as ... as\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The same\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">They are <span class=\\\"strong\\\">as tall as</span> each other.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"-er than\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"More\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">He is <span class=\\\"strong\\\">better than</span> his brother at soccer.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more than\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Much\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Kelly has done <span class=\\\"strong\\\">more than</span> her share of the cleaning.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"less than\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Fewer\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Susan has done <span class=\\\"strong\\\">less than</span> the others in the group.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"further than\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Farther\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">The team had been pushed <span class=\\\"strong\\\">further than</span> the other teams combined.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the more ... the more\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Increasing at the same time/rate\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">The more</span> things change <span class=\\\"strong\\\">the more</span> things stay the same.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals to Express Annoyance in the Past ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you want to express annoyance and criticism about the past, you can use modals. Modals such as <span class=\"strong\">could</span>, <span class=\"strong\">might</span>, <span class=\"strong\">should</span>, <span class=\"strong\">ought to</span>, and <span class=\"strong\">would not</span> add meaning to the main verb and can convey annoyance when you use them properly.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you talk about annoyance in the past, you use the modal + have + past participle. </br>Let's look at some modals and their meanings:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "1. <span class=\"strong\">Could have / Might have</span> - when you want to show you are are finding fault with someone's actions </br></br><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">could have said</span> something. </br>We <span class=\"strong\">might have been </span>told.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "2. <span class=\"strong\">Could have / Might have</span> - when you want to show that you are annoyed   </br></br><span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">might have apologized </span>for what you did. </br>She <span class=\"strong\">could have RSVP'd</span>, at least.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "3. <span class=\"strong\">Should have / Ought to have</span> - to criticize the choice the other person made  </br></br><span class=\"italic\">You<span class=\"strong\"> should have gone</span> to the doctor. </br>They <span class=\"strong\">ought to have finished </span>construction by now! </br>You <span class=\"strong\">should have submitted</span>  your project on time.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "4. <span class=\"strong\">Would not have</span> - when you say that your choice of what to do in a situation wasn't the same as another person's  </br></br> It <span class=\"strong\">wouldn't have hurt</span> him to pay for the dinner.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">might have</span> given me a heads up before lunch today. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Candace and I <span class=\"strong\">may have</span> had some correspondence about it back and forth.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You <span class=\"strong\">could have</span> informed me a little earlier.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">may have</span> known about your volunteering, but I just wish I could have been a part of your decision to go to Africa. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "heads up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "advance notice", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You might have given me a heads up before lunch today. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lucrative", "type": "name"}, {"content": "making a large amount of money", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This may be less lucrative than my other job.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rest assured", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to be \u200bcertain that something will \u200bhappen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Rest assured it is much more rewarding.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rewarding", "type": "name"}, {"content": "providing satisfaction; gratifying", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It is much more rewarding and important.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le16ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I research four idioms about anger and annoyance.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a PowerPoint presentation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I explain my idioms clearly and concisely.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use my idioms in sentences or conversations to help better explain.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a unique way to test my classmates knowledge.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, research four idioms or expressions about anger or annoyance.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a PowerPoint presentation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Your presentation should include the idiom and the meaning as well as images to help people understand the idiom better.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the idioms in a sentence or in a conversation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present your PowerPoint to the class.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The presentation should be about 5 minutes in length.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a unique way to test your classmates after about the idioms they just heard.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about beliefs, opinions, relationships or character traits.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express comparison between two things or events.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can express annoyance about an action or an event in the past.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What do you do when you are angry at someone?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What do you think people should do when they get angry?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " What do you do to avoid getting angry?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "t